  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-03-08T08:30:25.382Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Right now when using \"Measure by armspan\" and increasing it to avoid too short arms, your viewpoint tends to go down almost into your chest. It seems like it is still prioritizing that your real feet is on the ground, even when using armspan scaling. I would have expected it instead to give me a little amount of \"stilts\" to make sure my head and shoulders are still in the right place.\nAs a workaround, I have found that using playspace mover to adjust my viewpoint height back to something sensible yields pretty OK results. As long as I do not reset the offset, where my feet will go through the ground of course.\nNote this is possible since I use `--legacy-fbt-calibration` so my avatar isn't locked to head position during calibration.",
